review_comments.body:
The second `Load` isn't needed. Keep the result of the `Load` on line 93 and probe when it was unknown. The answer depends only on the filesystem, so an upload that raced another probe just gets the same result. The first commit's bug came only from re-reading the map after the open.

```go
supported, known := p.otmpXattr.Load(bucket)
if known && !supported.(bool) {
	return p.openMkTemp(...)
}
// open O_TMPFILE ...
if !known && xattrMeta {
	switch err := probeTmpFileXattr(f); {
	case err == nil:
		p.otmpXattr.Store(bucket, true)
	case tmpfileXattrUnsupported(err):
		p.otmpXattr.Store(bucket, false)
		f.Close()
		return p.openMkTemp(...)
	}
}
```
